  ('keystone-colorado', '12A', 'Keystone', 'United States', 'Colorado''s biggest night skiing and the ultimate family mountain', 'live', 'verified', 'northernLights', 'Mountain West', '{"ski","adventure","family","culinary","entertainment","romance","wellness"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'emerging', '{"key_facts":["Keystone = Vail Resorts / Epic; three mountains (Dercum, North Peak, The Outback) + Bergman/Erickson bowls; ~3,148 acres; vertical 3,128 ft (base 9,280 / summit 12,408); 21 lifts incl 2 gondolas","LARGEST night-skiing operation in Colorado (up to 15 lit trails + A51 park to 7 p.m.); A51 ~60-acre terrain park","~230 in (~5.8 m) snowfall + 660+ ac snowmaking; typically one of the first US resorts to open (25 Oct 2025) to ~5 Apr 2026","FAMILY-first: Kids Ski Free (12 & under, 2+ nights) + free Kidtopia (cookie time, parade, fireworks) + world''s largest mountaintop snow fort","CAT-SKIING HAS ENDED: the Bergman/Erickson bowls are now LIFT-SERVED by the Bergman Bowl Express (2023-24), 550+ ac in-bounds; no active paid cat-ski program","Purpose-built base-village complex (River Run + Mountain House/Lakeside) - NOT a historic town; no natural hot springs on-site (nearest ~1 hr)","US-TRAFFIC CANDOR: ~#9 nationally / ~1.4M is industry consensus, not operator-published","Fine dining Alpenglow Stube (11,444 ft) + Ski Tip Lodge (1800s prix-fixe); new upscale Kindred Resort (2025-26); DEN ~90 mi via I-70; ~14 mi to Breckenridge (not 6)"],"safety":{"emergency":"911 (police/fire/medical/rescue dispatch); alert ski patrol on-mountain; base emergency clinic in winter","hospital":"St. Anthony Summit Hospital, Frisco (~30 min) - 24/7 Level III trauma, Flight for Life base","malaria":"none","yellow_fever":"not required","activity_note":"ALTITUDE (base ~9,280 ft, summit 12,408 ft - AMS real; acclimatize, hydrate, ease alcohol, descend if worsening); AVALANCHE backcountry - CAIC ''Vail & Summit County'' zone daily bulletin (by ~4:30 PM), beacon/probe/shovel + guide, never duck ropes (in-bounds Bergman/Erickson bowls are patrolled/avalanche-controlled); tree-wells; night-ski flat-light + deep cold; I-70 Traction Law (Sept 1-May 31, Dotsero-Morrison) escalates to Chain Law - check CDOT cotrip.org","fcdo":{"posture":"1","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/usa","read":"2026-08-20T14:47:42Z","page_updated":"2026-08-18T10:29:04+01:00","source_country":"usa","quotes_note":"not extracted by the join — a restricted-area clause is quoted by a human, never composed"},"posture":"book-freely"},"timing":{"peak":"High winter (Christmas/NY, MLK, Presidents'', Feb-Mar, spring break); family holiday windows are the biggest crowds","shoulder":"early season (late Oct-mid Dec, often first to open), Jan midweek, April spring skiing","green":"May + late Oct-early Nov lull (lowest rates)","booking_lead":"Christmas/NY + Presidents'' + ski-in/out condos 3-6 mo; family peaks 3-6 mo; midweek/shoulder 2-6 wk; Epic Pass by early fall","off_season_specials":"night-ski + Kids-Ski-Free family packages; April spring skiing; midweek value; early-open November","event_peaks":"Christmas/NY, MLK + Presidents'', spring break, Kidtopia Signature Events (Spectacular/Culinary/Music - verify dates)","fire_date":"FIRE spring early-bird (Apr-Jun) Epic renewals + family pre-sell; fire again Sep-Nov leaning on early-open + night-ski + Kids-Ski-Free"},"jewels":[{"name":"Ski three linked mountains on one pass","si_tag":"Winter/Ski","status":"live","tier":"comfort","price_band":"window ~USD 169-269/day (dynamic); package far better value","timing":"ski late Oct-Apr","draw_rank":1,"hook":"Dercum, North Peak and The Outback plus the Bergman/Erickson bowls","si":"ski","blurb":"Dercum, North Peak and The Outback plus the Bergman/Erickson bowls","when":"ski late Oct-Apr","commission":"DMC/ski-op 10-15% (embedded-capable)","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["ski"],"shelf_fit":{"adventur