  ('mt-baker-washington', '12A', 'Mt. Baker Ski Area', 'United States', 'The mountain that holds the world snowfall record', 'live', 'verified', 'northernLights', 'Pacific Northwest', '{"ski","entertainment","culinary","romance"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'core', '{"key_facts":["Holds the NOAA-verified WORLD RECORD single-season snowfall — 1,140 inches, winter 1998-99 (beat Mt. Rainier''s 1,122 in 1971-72); the most snow ever verifiably recorded anywhere in one season","Averages ~641 in/yr — among the highest of any ski resort on Earth","Fiercely INDEPENDENT — no Epic, no Ikon; lift ticket is a direct product, not a pass loss-leader","1,000+ acres, 38 marked runs, 8 fixed-grip lifts; base ~3,500 ft, top ~5,089 ft, ~1,500 ft vertical","Set between Mt. Baker (10,781 ft active glaciated volcano) and Mt. Shuksan (9,131 ft) — one of the most-photographed mountain scenes in North America","Home of the Legendary Banked Slalom (snowboarding''s storied grassroots race, since 1985; canceled 2026 on conditions; 2027 targeted ~19-21 Feb)","NO on-mountain lodging — base town Glacier (~17 mi down SR-542); wider beds Bellingham (~55 mi/~1.5 hr); BLI nearest airport, SEA ~3 hr"],"safety":{"emergency":"911 (police/fire/ambulance/rescue dispatch, nationwide); ski patrol on-mountain; backcountry via Whatcom County SAR / 911","hospital":"PeaceHealth St. Joseph Medical Center (Bellingham) — 24/7 ER + regional trauma center, ~55 mi/~1.5 hr down SR-542; serious backcountry casualties airlifted; Glacier has no hospital","malaria":"none","yellow_fever":"not required","activity_note":"AVALANCHE beyond ropes (acute — deepest maritime snowpack in the country; huge lift-accessed backcountry; check NWAC nwac.us, guide-only + beacon/probe/shovel + Baker access policy); STEEP no-fall freeride terrain (expert, helmet, within-limit); TREE WELLS + deep snow (acute/heightened — deepest snow in the country, ride with partner); SR-542 winter access + chain control + gate closures above Glacier (check WSDOT); cold + fast Pacific storms + whiteouts; volcanic/glaciated alpine setting (Mt. Baker volcano + Shuksan scenery + serious off-resort terrain); AMS not a practical concern (top ~5,089 ft)","fcdo":{"posture":"1","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/usa","read":"2026-08-20T14:47:42Z","page_updated":"2026-08-18T10:29:04+01:00","source_country":"usa","quotes_note":"not extracted by the join — a restricted-area clause is quoted by a human, never composed"},"posture":"book-freely"},"timing":{"peak":"Deep winter Jan-Mar (powder); Christmas/NY, MLK + Presidents'' wknds; Legendary Banked Slalom weekend (typically Feb); big-storm cycles; weekends busiest (Bellingham/Vancouver BC + Seattle catchment)","shoulder":"early season (Dec pre-holidays), Jan weekdays, Apr spring snow (long on the big base)","green":"May-Nov (mountain closed outside snow season; SR-542 corridor quiet; some summer hiking/climbing traffic, no ski ops)","booking_lead":"Banked Slalom + Christmas/NY + best Glacier cabins 3-8 mo (small bed base fills fast); Presidents''/Feb + peak powder 2-5 mo; midweek/powder 1-4 wk","off_season_specials":"Apr spring-snow deals on big late base; midweek powder-chase packages; Bellingham + Salish Sea shoulder breaks paired with a Baker day; Banked Slalom + freeride-clinic weeks as event anchors","event_peaks":"Legendary Banked Slalom (typically Feb — 2027 targeted ~19-21 Feb; canceled 2026 on unworkable conditions), Christmas/NY, MLK + Presidents'' wknds, US + BC school half-terms","fire_date":"No pass conglomerate to time against — lead with snow. FIRE ski mid-late Mar (ahead of Apr-Jun early-bird) + late Aug-early Sep (ahead of Sep-Nov fall wave); push Banked Slalom from Sep-Oct (ahead of Feb event window)"},"jewels":[{"name":"Ski the world''s snowfall-record mountain in a deep cycle","si_tag":"Winter / Ski","status":"future","tier":"essential","price_band":"~USD 65-99/day lift; package the stay","timing":